{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1715","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1715","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1715\",\"parent_revision\":\"ab8c1ea74f92649f33424dadc129e20370b17915\",\"root_revision\":\"fc62ccfae344bb19883330d1ea0bf7a69f1c27d79ff23632a662d92aea558019\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe grooming swarm defined in swarm.md references two teammates \u2014 rtica-assessor and classifier \u2014 that have never existed as agent files anywhere in this repository's git history. The swarm's dependency graph makes the groomer teammate block on both of them, so the parallel swarm never completes a full grooming cycle and backlog items stuck on status:needs-grooming (observed on #1705) are never transitioned to status:groomed. Additionally, the name drift between swarm.md (classifier) and backlog-item-lifecycle.md (issue-classifier) means any future implementation picking one name breaks the other document.\\n\\nThis backlog item exists to retroactively track the work that should have accompanied commit f8c3acc4 (2026-03-15 feat(skills): redesign grooming as parallel swarm with team communication) when the parallel swarm concept was introduced. That commit modified SKILL.md documenting 5 teammates but added no new agent files, leaving rtica-assessor and classifier as phantom references from inception.\\n\\nThe role contracts for both agents are fully specified in swarm.md and are sufficient to implement from, but no implementation has ever been attempted. The phantom teammates have also leaked into #964's RT-ICA section as fabricated citations (agents claiming rtica-assessor performed research it could not have performed because it does not exist) \u2014 a hallucination risk that compounds the deeper problem.\\n\\nThe impact is every groomed backlog item on the repo since 2026-03-15 has depended on a broken swarm that cannot complete its dependency graph.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1**: rtica-assessor and classifier have never existed as agent files anywhere in this repository's git history\\n**Verdict**: PARTIALLY REFUTED (time-scoped)\\n**Evidence**: Both files exist as of 2026-04-13 \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` (161 lines) and `plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md` (146 lines). The claim was accurate at the time the item was filed (2026-04-12) but is now stale.\\n**Source**: Direct file read, confirmed present.\\n\\n**Claim 2**: Name drift exists between swarm.md (classifier) and backlog-item-lifecycle.md (issue-classifier)\\n**Verdict**: REFUTED\\n**Evidence**: `backlog-item-lifecycle.md` lines 211, 243, 256, 257 all use `classifier`. The term `issue-classifier` does not appear anywhere in the codebase (grep confirmed zero matches).\\n**Source**: `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`\\n\\n**Claim 3**: Items at status:needs-grooming are never transitioned to status:groomed because of the broken swarm\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED (mechanism confirmed; current state after fix is DERIVABLE)\\n**Evidence**: swarm.md line 40 declares `groomer \u2192 blocked by rtica-assessor + classifier`. Absent either agent file, the groomer could never fire. With both files now present, the swarm can complete.\\n**Source**: `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md` lines 39-40\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Goal**: Create the missing rtica-assessor and classifier agent files so the grooming swarm can complete its dependency graph end-to-end.\\n**Assessed**: 2026-04-13\\n\\n**Conditions**:\\n\\n| # | Condition | State | Evidence or derivation path |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | rtica-assessor agent file exists | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` \u2014 file present, 161 lines, complete role contract |\\n| 2 | classifier agent file exists | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md` \u2014 file present, 146 lines, complete role contract |\\n| 3 | swarm.md dependency graph references both agents | AVAILABLE | `swarm.md` lines 17-22, 38-40 \u2014 both teammates listed with correct wave assignments |\\n| 4 | backlog-item-lifecycle.md uses consistent agent names | AVAILABLE | `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` lines 211-213, 243-246 \u2014 uses `classifier` and `rtica-assessor` consistently; `issue-classifier` does not appear anywhere in the codebase |\\n| 5 | Both agent files conform to plugin frontmatter schema | DERIVABLE | Run `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md` |\\n| 6 | Grooming swarm completes a full cycle end-to-end | DERIVABLE | Run the grooming swarm on a test item and confirm all 6 sections are written without groomer hanging |\\n| 7 | #964 RT-ICA section no longer contains fabricated rtica-assessor citations | DERIVABLE | `backlog_view(\\\"#964\\\", sections=[\\\"RT-ICA\\\"])` and verify citations reference actual tool output |\\n| 8 | Items at status:needs-grooming (e.g. #1705) can now complete grooming | DERIVABLE | Run grooming on #1705 and confirm it transitions to status:groomed |\\n\\n**Counts**: AVAILABLE 4, DERIVABLE 4, MISSING 0\\n**Verdict**: READY\\n\\n**Note**: The item description claims both agents were never created \u2014 this was accurate at filing time (2026-04-12) but is stale. Both agent files exist as of grooming date 2026-04-13. The remaining work is end-to-end validation, not initial creation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **feat: create missing rtica-assessor and classifier agents to unblock grooming swarm** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Investigation of #1705 \u2014 grooming swarm teammates rtica-assessor and classifier referenced in plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md and plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md have never existed as agent files in git history across 74 refs. Origin commit f8c3acc4 (2026-03-15) introduced the parallel swarm design naming 5 teammates but only 3 (impact-analyst, fact-checker, backlog-item-groomer) had corresponding agent files. The other 2 (rtica-assessor, classifier) were documented in prose but never implemented. Dangling references mean the grooming swarm cannot run end-to-end: groomer is blocked by rtica-assessor + classifier per swarm.md:40, so mark_groomed=True is never called, so status:needs-grooming never transitions to status:groomed \u2014 the observed symptom in #1705.\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-13)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Checkout the repository at any commit between f8c3acc4 (2026-03-15) and the commit that added rtica-assessor.md and classifier.md\\n2. Invoke the grooming swarm on any item with status:needs-grooming\\n3. Observe that Wave 1 completes (impact-analyst, fact-checker, classifier fire and write sections)\\n4. Observe that Wave 2 never starts \u2014 rtica-assessor has no agent file, the swarm cannot spawn it\\n5. Observe that groomer never fires and the item remains at status:needs-grooming indefinitely\\n\\nNote: Reproduction requires a historical checkout. In the current working tree both agent files exist and the swarm can complete.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Every backlog grooming operation since 2026-03-15 that used the parallel swarm path was silently broken. Items accumulate at status:needs-grooming without ever completing. This is not a cosmetic issue \u2014 it breaks the core automated grooming workflow and compounds hallucination risk in downstream planning. P1 is correct.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Every backlog item that reaches grooming stage using STANDARD or FULL scope \u2014 the groomer never fires, status never transitions from needs-grooming to groomed\\n- Bottleneck: The groomer teammate in Wave 3 depends on both rtica-assessor (Wave 2) and classifier (Wave 1) completing; neither could be spawned without their agent files\\n- Compounding: Hallucinated rtica-assessor citations in #964's RT-ICA section create downstream false signals for planning agents that read that item\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Grooming swarm can now run end-to-end: all 6 teammates complete, items transition to status:groomed\\n- Removes a hallucination risk class: agents no longer fabricate output from non-existent teammates\\n- Unblocks items currently stuck at status:needs-grooming that failed because the swarm DAG could not be satisfied\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a grooming swarm runs on a backlog item at STANDARD or FULL scope: Wave 1 spawns impact-analyst, fact-checker, and classifier in parallel; Wave 2 spawns rtica-assessor and alignment-analyst after Wave 1 completes; Wave 3 spawns groomer after Wave 2 completes. All teammates write their respective sections via MCP. The item transitions from status:needs-grooming to status:groomed.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` exits 0\\n2. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md` exits 0\\n3. Run the grooming swarm on a test item at STANDARD scope: Fact-Check, Impact Radius, Issue Classification, RT-ICA, Design Intent Alignment, and at least one groomed subsection are all written to the item via MCP\\n4. The test item transitions from status:needs-grooming to status:groomed after the swarm completes\\n5. `backlog_view(\\\"#964\\\", sections=[\\\"RT-ICA\\\"])` returns an RT-ICA section that does not contain fabricated citations attributing research output to rtica-assessor\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Agent | @dh:rtica-assessor \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` |\\n| Agent | @dh:classifier \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md` |\\n| Agent | @dh:backlog-item-groomer \u2014 groomer that was blocked; now unblocked |\\n| Workflow | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md` \u2014 swarm dependency graph |\\n| Workflow | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/start.md` \u2014 groom start workflow |\\n| Workflow | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/analyze.md` \u2014 scope tier definitions |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 lifecycle doc with correct agent names |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 both agent files now exist; remaining work is validation only\\n- Blocks: Any backlog item currently at status:needs-grooming that failed because of the broken swarm (notably #1705)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 Both agent files already exist. Remaining work is: run skilllint validation on both files (minutes), run one end-to-end grooming swarm to confirm completion (one agent spawn), and correct the fabricated citation in #964 (one MCP write call).\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` \u2014 the groomer agent; now has its blocking dependencies satisfied\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md` \u2014 declares both agents as teammates; now satisfiable\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/start.md` \u2014 lines 55-58 reference both agents by name\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/analyze.md` \u2014 lines 150-151 include both in STANDARD and FULL scope tiers\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` \u2014 the new agent file; produces RT-ICA assessments for the grooming swarm\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md` \u2014 the new agent file; produces Issue Classification and Root-Cause Analysis sections\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 lines 211-213, 241-258 document both teammates; no change needed, names already match\\n- GitHub Issue #964 \u2014 RT-ICA section contains fabricated citations attributing research to rtica-assessor (which could not have performed research before this fix). Needs correction.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [x] Both agent files created (rtica-assessor.md, classifier.md)\\n- [ ] Both agent files pass skilllint validation\\n- [ ] Grooming swarm runs end-to-end on a test item without groomer blocking\\n- [ ] #964 RT-ICA section corrected to remove fabricated rtica-assessor citations\\n- [ ] Items at status:needs-grooming that failed due to broken swarm can now complete (verify on #1705)\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n**Rationale**: The parallel grooming swarm documented in swarm.md referenced two teammates (rtica-assessor, classifier) that had never been implemented as agent files. The dependency graph declared `groomer \u2192 blocked by rtica-assessor + classifier`, so the groomer could never fire and `mark_groomed=True` was never reached. This is a traceable failure with an identifiable cause chain, and a reproduction command can exercise it (spawn the swarm on any item, observe groomer never fires).\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys\\n**Scenario Target**: grooming swarm launches but groomer teammate never fires (blocked indefinitely) \u2192 grooming swarm runs all 6 teammates to completion and item transitions to status:groomed\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys\\n**Evidence chain**:\\n1. Observed failure: Items accumulate at status:needs-grooming and never transition to status:groomed (observed: #1705)\\n2. Why: The groomer teammate, which calls `mark_groomed=True`, never fires\\n3. Why: groomer is declared as blocked by `rtica-assessor + classifier` in swarm.md line 40; both must complete before groomer starts\\n4. Why: rtica-assessor and classifier had no corresponding agent files \u2014 the swarm could not spawn them, so their completion signal never arrived\\n5. Why: commit f8c3acc4 (2026-03-15) redesigned the grooming workflow to reference these two teammates in prose and documentation but did not create the agent files as part of the commit\\n\\n**Root cause**: The parallel swarm redesign commit documented two new teammate roles without creating the agent files that implement them, leaving the swarm DAG permanently unsatisfiable.\\n**Fix locus**: `plugins/development-harness/agents/` \u2014 both files now created. Remaining verification: confirm swarm runs end-to-end and #964's RT-ICA section is corrected.\\n\",\"digest\":\"912c5ea15800fe683bd181760bd49aa98cf970ce46260966b179f6029f352ff0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnI11w\"}"}